WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.050
Parts of the Amazon rainforest have
stood for tens of millions of years.

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.290
Populations rise and fall.

3
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.600
Trees die and are replaced.

4
00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:12.560
Yet the same kind of forest persists.

5
00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:17.710
About 17 per cent of the original
forest had been cleared by 2021.

6
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:23.590
So if people clear part of a rainforest,
could the rest of it dry out and die?

7
00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:28.150
In this mission, you'll see how ecologists
test stability with a sealed glass

8
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.960
jar of pond life.

9
00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:34.770
Then you'll see what happened on a rocky
shore when one starfish was removed:

10
00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:38.000
species fell from 15 to 8.

11
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:42.690
Your mission: find out whether clearing
part of a rainforest could make the rest

12
00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:44.040
dry out and die.
